{"name":"Cookies and Cream","hex":"#eee0b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cookies and Cream","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flavor of ice cream made by combining vanilla or sweet cream ice cream with chunks of chocolate cookie (often Oreos)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cookies_and_Cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cookies and cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cookies and cream is a variety of ice cream, milkshake, and other desserts, including chocolate sandwich cookies, with the most popular version containing hand or pre-crumbled cookies from Nabisco's Oreo brand under a licensing agreement, or else, containing crumbles of a similar cookie of a different brand or private label. Cookies and cream ice cream generally mixes crumbled chocolate sandwich cookies into vanilla ice cream. However, variations exist which instead use chocolate, coffee or mint ice cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Cookies_and_cream.JPG/330px-Cookies_and_cream.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cookies_and_cream"},{"title":"Cookie","blocks":[{"text":"A cookie is a sweet biscuit with high sugar and fat content. Cookie dough is softer than that used for other types of biscuit, and they are cooked longer at lower temperatures. The dough typically contains flour, sugar, egg, and some type of oil or fat. It may include other ingredients such as raisins, oats, chocolate chips, or nuts. Cookie texture varies from crisp and crunchy to soft and chewy, depending on the exact combination of ingredients and methods used to create them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg/330px-2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cookie"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Udders_Cookies_and_Cream_Ice_Cream.jpg/500px-Udders_Cookies_and_Cream_Ice_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Udders_Cookies_and_Cream_Ice_Cream.jpg/1280px-Udders_Cookies_and_Cream_Ice_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Udders_Cookies_and_Cream_Ice_Cream.jpg/500px-Udders_Cookies_and_Cream_Ice_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cookies and Cream Ice Cream","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUdders_Cookies_and_Cream_Ice_Cream.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/R%C5%AFzn%C3%A9_druhy_cukrov%C3%AD_%282%29.jpg/500px-R%C5%AFzn%C3%A9_druhy_cukrov%C3%AD_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/R%C5%AFzn%C3%A9_druhy_cukrov%C3%AD_%282%29.jpg/1280px-R%C5%AFzn%C3%A9_druhy_cukrov%C3%AD_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/R%C5%AFzn%C3%A9_druhy_cukrov%C3%AD_%282%29.jpg/500px-R%C5%AFzn%C3%A9_druhy_cukrov%C3%AD_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dish of assorted cookies, including sandwich cookies filled with jam","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AR%C5%AFzn%C3%A9_druhy_cukrov%C3%AD_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Biscits_or_cookiess.jpg/500px-Biscits_or_cookiess.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Biscits_or_cookiess.jpg/1280px-Biscits_or_cookiess.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Biscits_or_cookiess.jpg/500px-Biscits_or_cookiess.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cookies baking in an oven","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABiscits_or_cookiess.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Holiday_Cookie_Tray.jpg/500px-Holiday_Cookie_Tray.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Holiday_Cook